# libubootenv (fw_printenv / fw_setenv) config for the Beep's U-Boot environment.
#
# ⚠️ GEOMETRY IS INFERRED, NOT YET PROVEN. It must pass a bench round-trip before the
# good-boot bootcount reset is enabled (create /etc/beep-fwenv-verified only after).
# A WRONG size here can make fw_setenv reinitialize the env to U-Boot's COMPILED
# defaults, whose beep_primary/beep_recovery are the *stock* offsets
# (0x9f550000 / 0x9f050000) — on our layout that is a BRICK. The reset script refuses
# to write unless `fw_printenv -n beep_primary` reads back 0x9f050000 through this
# config, which is the guard against a bad guess. Prove it on a UART unit first:
#     fw_printenv beep_primary        # must print 0x9f050000 (good CRC + right size)
#     fw_setenv beep_probe 1 && fw_printenv beep_probe   # round-trip
#     # then confirm on serial that the bootcount region (0x8000-0xFFFF) went to 0xFF
#
# Derived (docs/RECOVERY-DESIGN.md "Bootcount — decoded empirically"): u-boot-env is
# mtd1 @ flash 0x040000, one 64K sector. Env data occupies the first 32K (its own CRC);
# the wear-leveled bootcount uses the second 32K (0x8000-0xFFFF, 0xFF-padded). So
# CONFIG_ENV_SIZE is inferred = 0x8000, and any fw_setenv erases the 64K sector and
# rewrites 32K of env -> the bootcount half returns to 0xFF = reset.
#
# NOTE: /dev/mtd1 assumes the stock mtd order (mtd0 u-boot, mtd1 u-boot-env). If a
# variant reorders partitions this must be re-pointed by name from /proc/mtd.
#
# MTD device   Device offset   Env. size   Flash sector size
/dev/mtd1      0x0000          0x8000      0x10000
